": "Algiers, Algeria", "role": "Setting"}, {"name": "Paris, France", "role": "Cultural hub"}, {"name": "Oran, Algeria", "role": "Cultural context"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: The Stranger", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "the-stranger"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q163297", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Stranger_(Camus_novel)"], "tags": ["literary work", "Novels & Prose Fiction", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "The Stranger left a notable mark on Modern history, documented across 83 Wikipedia editions worldwide. Key lasting impacts include: Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission. Their legacy is studied through the lens of historical causation.", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": ""The Stranger" significantly impacted the trajectory of existential literature and philosophical thought, influencing generations of writers and thinkers and shaping the discourse on meaning and morality in the 20th century.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-06-08T14:01:35Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27142557986", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "1942 novel by albert camus Created by Albert Camus. Created c. 1940.", "newValue": ""The Stranger," published in 1942, is a seminal work of existential literature authored by French-Algerian writer Albert Camus. Set against the backdrop of Algeria, the novel explores themes of absurdism and the human condition. It emerged in a period marked by World War II and the existential crises that accompanied it, making it a crucial text within the Modernist literary canon. Camus's protagonist, Meursault, embodies the alienation and existential indifference that many felt in the tumultuous early 20th century, reflecting broader societal disillusionment with traditional moral frameworks.

The narrative unfolds around Meursault, who lives a seemingly detached life until he commits an act of violence that leads to his trial. The courtroom scenes, which are a pivotal part of the novel, critique societal norms and the arbitrary nature of justice. Camus’s incisive prose and philosophical depth provided readers with a lens through which to examine the absurdity of life. The novel's famous closing line encapsulates its essence: "I could feel the anger rising within me, like a tide that would soon overflow its banks."

The legacy of "The Stranger" extends far beyond its initial publication; it has influenced countless writers, philosophers, and thinkers, shaping the discourse on absurdism and existentialism. It has been translated into numerous languages and remains a key text in literature and philosophy courses worldwide. The book's impact is evident in the post-war existentialist movement, influencing figures such as Jean-Paul Sartre and even later cultural critiques of modernity."}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T14:01:35Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27142557986", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": ["Cultural, artistic, or intellectual creation"], "newValue": ["The rise of existential philosophy in the early 20th century created a fertile ground for Camus's themes.", "The societal upheaval caused by World War II prompted a reevaluation of traditional moral values.", "French colonial rule in Algeria influenced Camus's perspective on identity and alienation."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T14:01:35Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27142557986", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": ["Contributed to cultural heritage and knowledge transmission"], "newValue": [""The Stranger" catalyzed the popularity of existential literature in the post-war era.", "The novel contributed to the broader philosophical discourse on absurdism and the human experience.", "Camus's work laid the groundwork for discussions about the nature of justice and morality in modern society."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-06-08T14:01:35Z", "editorId": "gpt-4o-mini·cloud·GH#27142557986", "field": "detailsJson.relationships", "oldValue": [{"sourceSlug": "the-stranger", "sourceName": "The Stranger", "verb": "OCCURS_DURING", "targetSlug": "era-modern", "targetName": "Modern", "context": "The Stranger is situated within the Modern (950)"}], "newValue": [{"sourceSlug": "albert-camus", "sourceName": "Albert Camus", "verb": "CREATES", "targetSlug": "the-stranger", "targetName": "The Stranger", "context": "Alber